    "whole": "Tabletop Bingo is a four-bar tabletop breakbeat. Under a canvas booth by the silt bank, a denim-pocketed child watches a striped caterpillar crawl up a pyramid of sugar pumpkin candies. The caller taps the wire cage with a chisel, calls bingo, and the fluffy prize blimp bobs up and settles. The cage supplies the offbeat keyring, the rise and fall supplies the three-note bell question and lower answer, and the hovering prize supplies the light ceramic chord tails.",
